\subsubsection{Theory: Text summarization}
This task involves the process of creating a new text from the contents of the original text. This is one of the primary text generation tasks. There are two types of text summarization: abstractive and extractive summarization. The abstractive summarization method tries to paraphrase the given text with words not present in the original text. On the other hand, extractive summarization takes the main sentences from the original text and puts them together as a summary.

